                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "e86581a8-0d9c-4807-a639-2bcd78830299",
                        "source_entry_id": "d62a727f-d13b-34f2-9e33-01ac3eba9328",
                        "source_sense_id": "71d06300-d9eb-31bf-b9ac-ef95cf9ce086",
                        "target_lang_word": "insouciance",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "insouciance",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "0536c22a-f64b-3c88-8a9f-eb5bc89874c7",
                                        "entry_id": "9e27902b-c5f9-3999-b60c-c9021cb20c78",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Carelessness, heedlessness, indifference, or casual unconcern."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7cdfb9e4-7b58-4c07-b1a0-d58dc78ef5e4",
                                                "sense_id": "0536c22a-f64b-3c88-8a9f-eb5bc89874c7",
                                                "text": "So Gelernter, with an insouciance he now regrets, also chose a Lovelace as a namesake—Linda, the lead actress in \"Deep Throat.\""
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e431d892-59bd-3bb2-a1f3-d0dd957cfca7",
                                        "entry_id": "9e27902b-c5f9-3999-b60c-c9021cb20c78",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Nonchalance."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "497327c8-6cfa-4348-9124-280dff3c55d4",
                                                "sense_id": "e431d892-59bd-3bb2-a1f3-d0dd957cfca7",
                                                "text": "She almost felt insulted by [the wild boar's] insouciance as it rooted in her grove."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "90c62eb2-8896-485e-bfe1-8c2f720c4436",
                        "source_entry_id": "d62a727f-d13b-34f2-9e33-01ac3eba9328",
                        "source_sense_id": "71d06300-d9eb-31bf-b9ac-ef95cf9ce086",
                        "target_lang_word": "sprezzatura",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "sprezzatura",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "2b7462c8-2f3d-398c-939e-cd9594b567a2",
                                        "entry_id": "5ec6c514-35b3-3506-9a1e-f1cd280ca4dc",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The art of performing a difficult task so gracefully that it looks effortless; calculated nonchalance."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable",
                                            "usually"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5935eb3e-d833-476d-b2a9-55c61d1faa54",
                                                "sense_id": "2b7462c8-2f3d-398c-939e-cd9594b567a2",
                                                "text": "[…] I have found quite a universal rule which in this matter seems to me valid above all others, and in all human affairs whether in word or deed: and that is to avoid affectation in every way possible as though it were some very rough and dangerous reef; and (to pronounce a new word perhaps) to practice in all things a certain sprezzatura [nonchalance]^([sic]), so as to conceal all art and make whatever is done or said appear to be without effort and almost without any thought about it."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3c377f97-359f-42cd-8346-849376193e1f",
                                                "sense_id": "2b7462c8-2f3d-398c-939e-cd9594b567a2",
                                                "text": "Cassandra Wilson's music is the essence of sprezzatura, or calculated nonchalance, that special attitude described nearly 500 years ago by Baldassare Castiglione in “The Courtier,” his primer on how to ingratiate yourself with the aristocracy."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7737b25d-e43c-4093-9a11-97c2ef890c5d",
                                                "sense_id": "2b7462c8-2f3d-398c-939e-cd9594b567a2",
                                                "text": "Mr. Mork played with soulful intensity (and impeccable intonation), and the interplay between him and Mr. Repin, with nicely coordinated gestures and phrasings, was enjoyable to watch. But Mr. Repin’s technical struggles were all too evident — the very opposite of sprezzatura."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "49dd72c0-8bee-4c4d-85c5-d9c1b84f4a50",
                                                "sense_id": "2b7462c8-2f3d-398c-939e-cd9594b567a2",
                                                "text": "In men's fashion the ultimate style move is sprezzatura, embracing intentional errors such as undone buttons and misaligned neckties. Gianni Agnelli, the head of Fiat, wore watches over his shirtsleeves."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "02e6fbf6-6527-44c4-9b70-2352eca890ec",
                        "source_entry_id": "d62a727f-d13b-34f2-9e33-01ac3eba9328",
                        "source_sense_id": "71d06300-d9eb-31bf-b9ac-ef95cf9ce086",
                        "target_lang_word": "jauntiness",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "jauntiness",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "fe253644-ce09-39cf-9551-682015f553b3",
                                        "entry_id": "190ef235-48a6-3e43-a038-0900f130b8cc",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The quality of being jaunty."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "30432ac4-2204-4937-bb8c-435ed63c800e",
                                                "sense_id": "fe253644-ce09-39cf-9551-682015f553b3",
                                                "text": "\"That jauntiness of air I was once master of.\" - Joseph Addison"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "c315916a-7992-4947-a402-3b7c76362f9c",
                        "source_entry_id": "d62a727f-d13b-34f2-9e33-01ac3eba9328",
                        "source_sense_id": "71d06300-d9eb-31bf-b9ac-ef95cf9ce086",
                        "target_lang_word": "nonchalance",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "nonchalance",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "44642f90-9e93-304f-b746-15a5032e63ee",
                                        "entry_id": "d8bc8d8f-6e25-3060-b75d-3bac39d230b3",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Laisser-aller ; négligence ; apathie."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "bf6aa5b0-a2bd-49ae-b99b-46d858c917ab",
                                                "sense_id": "44642f90-9e93-304f-b746-15a5032e63ee",
                                                "text": "Elle était sobre, très propre et n’ayant d’autre défaut que beaucoup de paresse, la nonchalance régnant dans toutes ses actions et dans toute sa personne, malgré l’air de vivacité que ses yeux annonçaient."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e5e0f5d5-34c8-4529-9101-4d17d727bb2d",
                                                "sense_id": "44642f90-9e93-304f-b746-15a5032e63ee",
                                                "text": "Pour le reste, il avait laissé les choses suivre leur cours, et quand le vieux caissier, le vénérable Savourdin, bonhomme à lunettes d’or et à cravate blanche, le priait chaque soir de vérifier la caisse, il s’acquittait de cette besogne avec une nonchalance véritablement inexplicable."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c8f53ffd-ae70-4937-8fbb-29260681184b",
                                                "sense_id": "44642f90-9e93-304f-b746-15a5032e63ee",
                                                "text": "Je reconnaissais ce genre de plaisir qui requiert, il est vrai, un certain travail de la pensée sur elle-même, mais à côté duquel les agréments de la nonchalance qui vous fait renoncer à lui, semblent bien médiocres."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "49e30d0b-23c3-3544-b91e-647e9caa222c",
                                        "entry_id": "d8bc8d8f-6e25-3060-b75d-3bac39d230b3",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Mollesse ; langueur ; indolence."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f16b0b44-90e2-45e8-888c-e475a56c80cb",
                                                "sense_id": "49e30d0b-23c3-3544-b91e-647e9caa222c",
                                                "text": "Le soleil des tropiques, en brunissant son visage, ne lui avait point donné cette vivacité de geste et de parole qui s’unit chez les créoles à une nonchalance souvent pleine de grâce."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d8002e01-cf54-4656-9ac8-57fcfcff7c9e",
                                                "sense_id": "49e30d0b-23c3-3544-b91e-647e9caa222c",
                                                "text": "Penchés comme en une nonchalance de rêve sur les petits murs terreux, les amandiers pleurent leurs larmes blanches sous la caresse du vent..."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "75264e74-7312-403e-aed6-ec816ad8942a",
                                                "sense_id": "49e30d0b-23c3-3544-b91e-647e9caa222c",
                                                "text": "C'était un grand Noir filiforme qui semblait plein de nonchalance et de mauvaise volonté, bien qu'il portât une tunique à boutons et des culottes de nègre de maison."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "4102aca5-643e-313a-89bb-bb0f1348a3ce",
                                        "entry_id": "d8bc8d8f-6e25-3060-b75d-3bac39d230b3",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Relâchement, insouciance où l’on se complaît."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "literary",
                                            "plural"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "060bbfa9-c2dc-4c9e-83bb-3b46b5973f37",
                                                "sense_id": "4102aca5-643e-313a-89bb-bb0f1348a3ce",
                                                "text": "Ou je me réveillerai, et les lois et les mœurs auront changé, — grâce à son pouvoir magique, — le monde, en restant le même, me laissera à mes désirs, joies, nonchalances."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b8d02628-372f-4118-9f82-4f1c0f0ab52b",
                                                "sense_id": "4102aca5-643e-313a-89bb-bb0f1348a3ce",
                                                "text": "Mais non. Ce qu’il voulut, c’est arracher tous ceux\nQui vivaient engourdis, orgueilleux, paresseux,\nÀ l’égoïsme obscur, aux mornes nonchalances,\nPour les jeter, chantants et fiers, parmi les lances,\nIvres de dévouement, épris de mourir loin,\nDans cet oubli de soi dont tous avaient besoin !"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "5e8901b1-289b-4254-868c-162e56d57101",
                        "source_entry_id": "d62a727f-d13b-34f2-9e33-01ac3eba9328",
                        "source_sense_id": "71d06300-d9eb-31bf-b9ac-ef95cf9ce086",
                        "target_lang_word": "insouciance",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "insouciance",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "414b2b5c-e1a3-3546-8046-f0a3dd9e56e6",
                                        "entry_id": "a8909b6e-97ec-3b61-831a-58d762dc32b1",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "État ou caractère de celui qui est insouciant."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f0b89cc6-c0cd-4dd1-8adf-f6a772ea7c91",
                                                "sense_id": "414b2b5c-e1a3-3546-8046-f0a3dd9e56e6",
                                                "text": "Rien ne pouvait être entrepris sous la domination incontestée de Richard, […], quoiqu’il tînt les rênes du gouvernement avec une sorte d’insouciance qui tendait tantôt à l’indulgence et tantôt au despotisme."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f34b06aa-e503-4983-a437-e741503988ea",
                                                "sense_id": "414b2b5c-e1a3-3546-8046-f0a3dd9e56e6",
                                                "text": "Solange, jusqu’alors, avait toujours pris les événements de sa vie avec une certaine insouciance."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d45a7be3-762d-4be0-bff9-68a3013cfc80",
                                                "sense_id": "414b2b5c-e1a3-3546-8046-f0a3dd9e56e6",
                                                "text": "On leur dénie l’un des droits les plus fondamentaux de l’enfance : le droit à l’insouciance."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
